  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bath Iron Works has $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 19 awards, with an average award size of $112M and obligations down 10.3% year over year. Bath Iron Works shows a strong concentration in Ship Building and Repairing, which accounts for $2.1B of obligations in the current fiscal period. Bath Iron Works recorded obligations of $1B in FY21, $1.3B in FY22, $2.1B in FY23, $2.1B in FY24, and $2.4B in FY25 before the FY26 to date total of $2.1B. Bath Iron Works received 19 awards in the current period, indicating a portfolio of relatively large awards rather than many low-value contracts. Bath Iron Works also appears in other NAICS categories at much smaller scales, including Measuring, Dispensing, and Other Pumping Equipment Manufacturing at $37.6K and Convention and Trade Show Organizers at $27K. Current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date, and the largest industry concentration remains Ship Building and Repairing.",
